        "created_at": "2013-10-28T17:02:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I don't often have serious time for video games, but I used to really love the X-Com games. (I don't own a console and have two young kids, so the new reboot is not up for discussion.)&nbsp; I've instead found a nifty free open-source game that keeps the spirit of the old X-Com games while trying to update the story in a couple ways.</p><p>It deserves more exposure than it's gotten, and I'm contemplating trying to start a \"Let's Play\" thread for it either here or at VGG. These would not be videos, as I have no good recording capability and I much prefer text to video to allow people to ahve soldiers named after them or contribute to strategic discussions.</p><p>Would anybody here be interested in participating in such an event. (Incidentally, related to my attempt to post the Grasshopper's drawing of Absolute Zero, is there a way to post a picture directly from hard drive to forums without having to create a weblink for it?)</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:34.073Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
